---
import Terminal from "./Terminal.astro";
---

<section class="install" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="install-copy">
    <p class="section-tag"><span class="bubble">D</span>Section D-D · Assembly</p>
    <h2 id="install-title">One binary. <em>No setup.</em></h2>
    <ol class="general-notes">
      <li>
        Download the binary for your machine from the releases (Linux and macOS, x64 and arm64) and put it on
        your <code>PATH</code>.
      </li>
      <li>Swap in <code>linux-arm64</code>, <code>darwin-x64</code> or <code>darwin-arm64</code>.</li>
      <li>Then run <code>quench</code> with no arguments. It finds each harness home on its own, and only reads.</li>
      <li>
        <code>SHA256SUMS</code> in each release lists every binary's checksum. The macOS binaries are not signed; a
        copy downloaded with a browser needs <code>xattr -d com.apple.quarantine quench</code> before it runs.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="install-steps">
    <Terminal plate="D1" title="install">
      <span class="prompt">$</span> gh release download --repo JarenKempton/quench \{"\n"}    --pattern "quench-linux-x64" --output ~/.local/bin/quench{"\n"}<span class="prompt">$</span> chmod +x ~/.local/bin/quench{"\n"}<span class="prompt">$</span> quench --version</Terminal
    >
    <Terminal plate="D2" title="update">
      <span class="d"># update in place; uses the GitHub CLI</span>{"\n"}<span class="prompt">$</span> quench update{"\n"}<span class="prompt">$</span> quench update --channel nightly</Terminal
    >
  </div>
</section>
